  "model": "BACnet PTEC Unit Conditioner - Application 6644 (Two-Pipe Fan Coil Unit Cooling or Heating)",
  "model_slug": "ptec-6644-two-pipe-fan-coil",
  "short_model": "PTEC Two-Pipe Fan Coil 6644",
  "aliases": [
    "PTEC 6644",
    "Application 6644",
    "App 6644",
    "550-496PA",
    "Siemens 2-pipe fan coil",
    "Unit Conditioner"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Fan coil unit controller",
  "applies_to": "Two-pipe changeover fan coil units with one valve for heating or cooling and an optional second heating valve, on the Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller 550-496PA.",
  "summary": "Application 6644 runs a two-pipe fan coil unit on a Siemens BACnet PTEC unit conditioner controller over BACnet MS/TP. One valve serves heating or cooling depending on the water the plant supplies, an optional second valve adds heating, and the fan runs in day mode or cycles with demand. Heat/cool mode comes from a supply water pipe sensor (SUPPLY TEMP against COOL TEMP and HEAT TEMP) or a field panel command.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Newer than revision Bx40",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "AI and BI objects are read-only. AO and BO objects are BACnet output objects with a priority array; the guide has no access column, so access is inferred from object type. Many AOs are calculated status values, not commands.",
    "Instances shown in braces in the guide may be unbundled at a field panel; that marking is not reproduced here.",
    "Units are given in US units (°F); the guide also lists SI factory defaults.",
    "The guide covers controllers with firmware newer than revision Bx40; older firmware has separate documentation.",
    "The guide requires one of three heat/cool switchover methods: a supply pipe sensor, a commanded SUPPLY TEMP, or a commanded HEAT.COOL."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet PTEC Controller Unit Conditioner - Two-Pipe Fan Coil Unit Cooling or Heating, Application 6644, Application Note",
    "doc_number": "140-1171",
    "revision_date": "2015-03-31",
    "url": "https://sid.siemens.com/api/khub/documents/EgU6g84R6dfh5UBi29YtiQ/content"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Address the controller on the BACnet MS/TP trunk (manually or with auto addressing). The BMS commands occupancy with DAY.NGT (BO 29) and the day setpoints, sets heat/cool mode if no pipe sensor is fitted, and reads room temperature, fan status, valve position and the error status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 29",
        "name": "DAY.NGT",
        "why": "DAY = occupied, NIGHT = unoccupied"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 6",
        "name": "DAY CLG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied cooling setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 7",
        "name": "DAY HTG STPT",
        "why": "Occupied heating setpoint, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 5",
        "name": "HEAT.COOL",
        "why": "HEAT or COOL; command it if no pipe sensor"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BO 46",
        "name": "FAN",
        "why": "Fan on/off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 4",
        "name": "ROOM TEMP",
        "why": "Space temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 49",
        "name": "VLV 1 POS",
        "why": "Valve position, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 99",
        "name": "ERROR STATUS",
        "why": "Controller error code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Occupancy is DAY.NGT (BO 29). With a wall switch on DI 2 and WALL SWITCH (BO 18) = YES, the switch sets it; standalone with no switch the controller stays in day mode; on a network the field panel or BMS commands DAY.NGT. NGT OVRD (BO 21) shows a temporary night override from the room unit button.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "Without a supply pipe sensor, the field panel or PPCL either commands SUPPLY TEMP (AI 15) above HEAT TEMP or below COOL TEMP, or commands HEAT.COOL (BO 5) directly.",
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP only. CTLR ADDRESS (AO 1) holds the MS/TP address; the factory value is 255.",
      "APPLICATION (AO 2) holds the application number; the point table lists its factory default as 6691."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The guide's application notes state that the controller keeps all associated equipment OFF.",
      "With a digital room unit (revision 26 and later), a command sent through the room unit puts the matching BACnet input Out Of Service.",
      "Loop gains, motor timing, rotation angles and setup codes are commissioning values; don't write them from the BMS routinely."
    ]
  },
